ent-ClothingHandsLeatherGloves = leather gloves
    .desc = A pair of gloves, stitched together from cured leather.

ent-ClothingHandsFingerlessGloves = fingerless gloves
    .desc = Cloth gloves to absorb palm sweat while leaving the fingers free for fine manipulation.

ent-ClothingHandsClothwraps = bandages
    .desc = Thickly-woven bandages that've been wrapped around the hands. It soaks up the sweat from your palm, strengthens your fists, and protects your knuckles from dislodged teeth.

ent-ClothingHandsGauntlets = plate gauntlets
    .desc = A pair of alloyed gauntlets. Each finger is afforded a trinity of segments; with it, one can use a quill as precisely as an arming sword.

ent-ClothingHandsPaddedmitts = padded mittens
    .desc = A pair of gloves, quilted from cloth. Warmth for the pilgrim, reassurance for the laborer, and protection for the militiaman.

ent-ClothingHandsRoguegloves = fingerless leather gloves
    .desc = A pair of protective gloves favored by lockshimmers, laborers, and smokers for maintaining manual dexterity over regular gloves.

ent-ClothingHandsAgauntlets = decrepit plate gauntlets
    .desc = Rotted metal mechanisms, connected to form the shells of hands. Too clumsy to properly knock a bow, too rigid to comfortably grip a sword; clench those fists any tighter, and the segments'll cut into flesh.

ent-ClothingHandsBcgloves = bronze maille gauntlets
    .desc = Armored mittens, woven together from a series of interlinked bronze rings. It can comfortably accomadate the needs of a warrior in almost any action, be it stringing a longbow or wielding a sword.

ent-ClothingHandsBplategloves = blacksteel plate gauntlets
    .desc = Alloyed plate gauntlets, meticulously assembled from blacksteel. Each joint, a dozen segments; interconnected, interlinked, intertwined. Metal should not move so freely, like skin on flesh - yet it does.

ent-ClothingHandsFeldgloves = feldsher's gloves
    .desc = And when he woke up, his whole skeleton was missing, and the physicker was never heard of again! Ah, anyways; that's how I lost my writ of practice.

ent-ClothingHandsChainGloves = chain gauntlets
    .desc = Armored mittens, woven together from a series of interlinked steel rings. Articulation is difficult, but unnecessary; one would imagine these aren't the gloves of a tinkerer, after all.
